  <prompt>
    Close out the R4 project per the task-execute wrap-up protocol (root CLAUDE.md §7 project-close gate).
    This is the mandatory `090-wrapup` task — task-execute Step 11 invokes `/test-diet` BEFORE marking the
    project complete. Prescriptive close-out sequence:
    (1) Update `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/README.md` status → Complete.
    (2) Write `notes/lessons-learned.md` (R4-specific: the shadow-document rip-and-replace, the
        `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)` anchor model, the one-Patch-Engine consolidation, the
        Phase-0-gate-before-cutover discipline, and the hard-replace-with-no-A/B safety net).
    (3) Run `/test-diet` — the project-close test-diet gate (root §7): reconcile every test added/modified
        during R4 against the ADR-038 build-vs-maintain classifier (MAINTAIN stays at KEEP path, SCAFFOLDING
        is `git rm`, AMBIGUOUS → reviewer judgment). It is READ-ONLY — it emits `git rm`/`git mv` commands
        for the reviewer; do NOT auto-execute. Save the report to `notes/test-diet-report.md`.
    (4) Update the project's row in `projects/INDEX.md`.
    (5) Run `/repo-cleanup` (ephemeral-file hygiene).
    (6) Archive artifacts; set TASK-INDEX to all ✅; reset `current-task.md` to none.
    This is a wrap-up task — no new surface, no `&lt;justification&gt;`. The wrap-up PR MUST cite the /test-diet
    report. This task is TERMINAL — blocked until the flagship gate (063) is all-green.
  </prompt>

